rk in characters  like big mom's hunger pangs pudding's  powers and the wedding ceremony proper  to name but a few that play pivotal  roles in the second half of this tale  constantly in the second half it feels  like we're going from one major moment  to the next full of interesting  opportunities for these characters to  participate in and  interact with with two clear standout  scenes early on coming from luffy's  meeting with beji  that contained a few pages a little more  explicit than i'm comfortable with while  sitting around my fiance  and of course the big moment that was  established in the prior arcs of the  story  the wedding of sanji and pudding in fact  by the way something funny that i  noticed  on the cover of volume 86 we get a nice  image of pudding and sanji about to be  wet  note the eye contact and height  difference now  if you skip to chapter 862 you'll find  that corresponding artwork for this  volume itself with sanji instead of  looking into her eyes like the cover it  looks like he's looking at her boobs  even in moments of extreme stress he's  unable to restrain himself  classic but again this second half of  the story feels like it could be  categorized as its own arc  in the same way that water 7 and his  lobby were part of the same story threat  i understand one piece likes to name its  axe by the name of islands visited but  i mean they could have called it cacao  island or something i don't know  the meeting with benji is honestly  mostly for exposition and a bit of humor  with large amounts of the appeal coming  from luffy's interactions with beijing  himself and steve  who finds himself in capone's possession  which as it happens is a good thing  because he ends up playing a vital role  once again in the arc early concerning  the plan to crash sanji's wedding and to  foil their plans  however what i thought was interesting  concerning this portion of the story is  that luffy  indirectly becomes involved in a plan to  assassinate big mom  now that plan does involve aspects of  the big mom character we weren't privy  to prior to this plan  coming to light and so it feels more  like exposition rather than the reveal  of the plan first and foremost  a significant amount of focus regarding  this plan concerns the picture frame big  mom cherishes that acts also as the  impetus for one of the only flashbacks  proper in this part of the story  personally i didn't anticipate nor  think that big mom required a backstory  but now that we have one i suppose  i did enjoy certain parts from it and  after all whitebeard got one too and the  sections that i really enjoyed were  those that explored elbaf for the very  first time this was a place that we had  heard about during little garden and is  now a place we've finally seen  albeit in the distant past there's also  this rather  gruesome scene or at least i think it's  gruesome scene where we see a young big  mom devour a cake but also her entire  group of friends  and mother carmel i appreciate in some  respects the painting oda is trying to  capture for us in this flashback an  orphan that was never understood and  always put down  it's clear that big mom is misguided and  began with the best of intentions but  when we flash forward to the president  and see big mom hacking and slashing her  way through town after town after town  presumably killing people  including her own children by the way  i'm not sure if that flashback could be  as effective for me considering the  heinous act she's continuing to perform  even when not  under the trends of her hunger pang now  i do appreciate that it stands to make  her a slightly more nuanced than perhaps  a more interesting character taking the  if you were all judged on our worst day  that how good would any of us be sort of  approach but if your character has more  bad days than one can count and  is a literal tyrant it falls short in  making me gain sympathy for her in a lot  of respects  that is assuming that's what oda wanted  to do he might not have one of the most  hotly anticipated scenes from this  portion of the ark for me was the doomed  wedding of sanji and pudding  which totally lived up to the hype for  me by the way despite it acting as an  assassination attempt by both big mom's  forces and veggie  it has an enjoyable amount of sustained  tension with the countdown to the moment  it all goes down on it has some striking  visuals as i mentioned a crazy backstory  and more than enough comedy to add some  variety to stop the occasion from  getting a little too straightforward and  the best part is that like most plans  made in one piece  they don't go according to plan because  let's be honest  that'd be boring and i think in having  things go awry from the get-go not only  did it make for a much more interesting  and fleshed out occasion with the  wedding itself but it also  served to create a set of circumstances  afterwards that produce one of the  single best fight scenes i've seen in  the series as well as the foundations  for a structure that i found to be both  easy to understand  and exciting and there are numerous  highlights from this wedding from the  tense build-up to the planned enactment  to the sweet and tender moments shared  by sanji and pudding and of course the  hundreds of luffys exploding out of the  wedding cake  destroying it which as funny as it was  turns out to be one of the main missteps  in this arc because  big mom she'd be wanting some wedding  cake and she's gonna be saying that a  lot from this point on something else i  thought was worth mentioning was  something a friend of mine pointed out  to me once i encountered putting in the  story  apparently she was featured in chapter  651  that is hundreds of chapters ago which  again reinforces the notion that oda is  an absolute lunatic when it comes to  foreshadowing events in his story  and while we're on the topic of pudding  i have to say she really surprised me as  a character  while i wasn't super interested in her  goody two-shoes persona that was  presented to us early on  once it was revealed that she was just  evil the entire time i  wasn't really expecting anything too  interesting to come from her thereafter  but boy was i wrong once she  legitimately starts to fall for sanji  after he calls her third eye beautiful  the mental gymnastics this woman  performs in order to attempt to speak  and  rationalize with was one of the funniest  and most charming parts of this  arc for me with her also playing a  pivotal role in the side of good within  this part of the story  she's easily one of my favorite  characters introduced in any of the  islands we've visited since the  beginning  something that also came to my attention  during my time reading this was  how strange it must have felt reading  week to week for a lot of people  being exposed to only one half of the  straw hat crew at any given time  splitting them up in dressrosa and once  again in whole cake i'm  actively aware that i'm in a rather  unique position where i can dedicate  half of this year to catching up on this  series and as a result i  bulldozed through it i was only reading  the style of dress rosa a few weeks ago  but for some of you watching this you  must have gone  years without seeing some of these  characters you've grown up with and i  wonder what that must have been like  in saying that i thought punk hazard  suffered from having too many characters  and i definitely think splitting the  crew into a more focused group was a  good idea  but i bet there were a lot of you out  there that were during this time missing  zorro for the two years oda spent on  whole cake island i suppose i'll get an  idea of what that might be like as i get  caught up to this series later this year  back to the wedding however there's a  rather awesome set of circumstances that  sanji shares with his family and more  specifically  his father who when faced with the truth  of the occ